 "transcript": [
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung looks at his sons and then at Pear Blossom.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son returns home.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We are setting up a great store and we will make a great deal of money out of it.\"",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"We will sell out the lands and buy silver and gold and we will not be poor again,\"",
  "[action] Eldest son moves away from father with a mixture of anger and hatred",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) The second son leaves with his brother.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and those are my sons and they are my flesh and blood,\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung goes to room and sits on bed",
  "[says] (to the second son) Eldest son taunts his brother about his lack of ambition.",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"Well, and you may call me an official and you may boast of your store, but what do you do? You sit there and eat your rice and your meat and your wine and you do not even know the names of the rich men in the town,\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung hears the argument and goes to the room.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"What is all this about?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and what is it, my second son?\"",
  "[says] The second son denies taunting his brother.",
  "the second son (to the eldest son): \"That I did not. I was only saying what was in my heart. I was saying what you said yourself.\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung asks his son to explain his words.",
  "[says] The second son explains his words.",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"There are these rich men in the town and they do not work with their hands and they do not work with their heads. They do nothing, only sitting in their courts, spending their money and eating their rice and drinking their wine, and there they will sit until they die, doing nothing.\"",
  "[says] Eldest son defends his own life."
